Return a waiting result before decoding another step.

Every get_result call ran the server loop once and then returned one result of its own request.
With several requests in flight, each call so decoded a token for all of them and collected
one. The results piled up, and a caller saw the end of its request long after the server had
finished it. A result that is already waiting is now returned without running the loop.

diff --git a/cpp/wllama-context.h b/cpp/wllama-context.h
index 51682a6..29f890b 100644
--- a/cpp/wllama-context.h
+++ b/cpp/wllama-context.h
@@ -862,8 +862,18 @@ struct wllama_context
     }
     server_response_reader &rd = *it->second;
 
-    run_loop();
-    auto [result, is_error] = get_next_result(rd);
+    // A result that is already waiting for this reader is returned without decoding another
+    // step. When every poll ran the loop, each poll of one reader also produced a token for
+    // all the others, so their results piled up and a reader learned that its request had
+    // ended only once the whole group had.
+    auto next = get_next_result(rd);
+    if (!next.first && rd.has_next())
+    {
+      run_loop();
+      next = get_next_result(rd);
+    }
+    auto &result = next.first;
+    const bool is_error = next.second;
     // the task queue can be empty while the request is still streaming, keep polling until we get the stop result
     const bool has_more = rd.has_next();
 
